        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "Both approaches produce the same solution — the gravitational potential $u$\n",
        "induced by two mass concentrations located at $(0.25, 0.25)$ and\n",
        "$(0.70, 0.65)$.  The sparse solver handles $N = 80$ (6 400 unknowns) effortlessly,\n",
        "while the dense solver would require storing a $6400 \\times 6400$ matrix.\n",
        "For even larger systems one would switch to an iterative solver such as\n",
        "**conjugate gradients** (`spla.cg`) combined with an AMG or ILU preconditioner.\n",
